{
  "out": "/tmp/photonz-playtest/caliper-catches-a-drawn-edge",
  "seed": "A rectangle you drew yourself used to measure short: its outline is drawn inside its box, so a hand aiming at the line a person can see lands a little inside the box at each end, and nothing pulled it back. A 64 point box read 62. This walk draws a box, sets it to exactly 128 by 128 device pixels, and measures its height at three zooms with both feet deliberately aimed at the MIDDLE of that outline rather than at the box. Every reading has to be 64 points. The last stage measures a button in the picture underneath instead, to show that snapping to a screenshot is untouched.",
